From 0559063a67d453f7dab1a0a8405213fa52cd363e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ruscher <rruscher@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 18:50:27 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 23/24] dock: Adds `wlmdock --clip`, for launchers attached
 below the Clip.

In Window Maker, application icons can be attached to the Clip. Permits
the same for launchers (eg. web browser and file manager):

* The state file's `Clip` dictionary takes an optional `Launchers` array,
  in the same format as the Dock's. The Clip leaves room for them (one
  transparent tile per launcher) right after the Clip tile; dock-apps
  follow after those.
* `wlmdock --clip` reads the launchers from the `Clip` section instead of
  `Dock`, and places them over that room: Relative to the full output, not
  reserving an exclusive zone, at one tile's distance from the anchor.
* Both the Dock and the Clip section accept an optional `Margin`, the
  distance from the anchor in pixels. toolkit: wlmtk_dock_positioning_t has
  the new `margin` and `overlay` fields, applied by wlmtk_dock_t and by the
  layer surface of wlmdock.

Documents the state file's Dock and Clip keys in doc/config.md.

Signed-off-by: ruscher <rruscher@gmail.com>
---
